An array is a data structure used to store multiple values of the same data type in a single variable.

In simple terms, an array is like a collection of elements stored in continuous memory locations, where each element can be accessed using an index (position number).

Example:

If you want to store marks of 5 students, instead of creating 5 separate variables, you can use an array:

int marks[5] = {80, 75, 90, 85, 70};
Here:

marks is the array name
5 is the size of the array
Each value can be accessed using an index (starting from 0)
marks[0] = 80
marks[1] = 75
```